Description: base_unittests' SafeSPrintfTest.EmitNULL passes NULL where SafeSPrintf takes an integer or a pointer, which only works where C++'s NULL is integer-like (glibc's __null); musl's C++ NULL is nullptr, so the call is ambiguous and the test can't compile: Alpine leaves the test out.
Forwarded: not-needed (Alpine's musl patch; Alpine carries it)
Origin: Alpine Linux aports ecc3ce96955f459cf819602db39593b42ded8515, community/chromium/disable-failing-tests.patch
Applies as Alpine's does (its hunks sit 4 lines lower in this tarball: an offset, no fuzz).

